Key finding: the **red hat click is a toggle** — the 2nd click moved red back from B (middle-right, vertical) to D (center, horizontal), restoring the initial red position. So both hats are 2-state toggles:
- **Red hat**: red ↔ {D (center, horizontal) , B (mid-right, vertical)}
- **Blue hat**: blue square ↔ blue X between {A (top) , F (left-bottom)}
I've now seen all 4 hat-combination states and none completed the level, so the **player position must also matter**. The "ring" is actually a fixed 6×6 gray block (r38–43 c8–13) with the 2×2 green player embedded inside it. Let me check the bottom white bar (possible step timer) and test whether the player can exit the block by pressing UP.

